    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-general-2012-p1.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "28 We note that \\(25^{3}-27^{2}=5^{6}-3^{6}=\\left(5^{3}-3^{3}\\right)\\left(5^{3}+3^{3}\\right)=(5-3)\\left(5^{2}+5 \\cdot 3+3^{2}\\right)(5+\\) \\(3)\\left(5^{2}-5 \\cdot 3+3^{2}\\right)=2 \\cdot 7^{2} \\cdot 2^{3} \\cdot 19\\), so the sum of the distinct prime factors is \\(2+7+19=28\\).",
